course: dictionary
lesson: 15122
title: Sanctified: made holy or approved
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words are rare and formal, so they do not appear often in everyday talk. «Sanctified» is one of them. When you meet it, look at the words around it for clues. «The old church was sanctified by the bishop, so it became a holy place.» The bishop made the church holy, so sanctified means made holy.
explain: Sanctified also has a second, formal meaning. «The rule about sharing bread was sanctified by tradition, so everyone kept it.» Here nothing holy is happening. The rule was made acceptable because people had followed it for a very long time. Ask yourself what would fit: made holy, or approved by custom? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check.
explain: Sanctified is the past form of the verb sanctify. Sanctify, sanctifies, sanctified and sanctifying all come from the same root. When you see sanctified, it describes something that has already been made holy or approved.
fact: Sanctified means made holy or set apart for God in a religion.
fact: Sanctified can also mean made acceptable or approved, often by a long custom. This is the formal meaning.
fact: «Sanctified» is a rare, formal word, so it is often found in religious writing and in serious or old-fashioned texts.
fact: Context clues help: look for words like church, priest, tradition or custom near the word.
fact: A good check is to swap in a simpler word, such as holy or approved, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The church was sanctified by the bishop.» What does sanctified mean here? | Painted bright white | Closed for ever | *Made holy, set apart for God | Moved to a new town
exercise: «Sharing bread at the feast was sanctified by long tradition.» What does sanctified suggest? | Argued about in court | Made into a new rule overnight | *Made acceptable by long custom | Forgotten by everyone
exercise: Which word means nearly the same as sanctified in the religious sense? | Hungry | Sticky | *Holy | Loud
test: «The priest sanctified the water before the service.» What does sanctified mean? | Frozen solid | Dirty and warm | Poured into bottles | *Blessed and made holy
test: «The old rule was sanctified by tradition, so everyone kept it.» What does sanctified mean here? | *Approved by long custom | Written in a book | Forgotten last week | Broken by the new king
exam: «Church leaders said the sanctified ground could never be sold.» What does sanctified mean here? | Cheap and easy to buy | *Made holy and set apart for God | Very dusty and dry | Covered in snow
